producer_report.summary:
I created studies/firstmate-work-handling/ and a kept test that checks it against the real pinned tree. fmt, clippy and the full `cargo test --locked` all pass.

The study has pin.json with the full SHA 6407052f4c521e39401ce2305dfa45d201249827, 22 claims, 4 rationale cards, a small model (5 states, 8 transitions, 1 counter), and validation.json. It also has a sixth file, findings.json, which you didn't list. The rules need findings, and the study has no other place for them.

Every cited source is a file with path, line range, the full SHA and a verbatim quote. All claims are marked `read`, because nothing was run. Each claim text starts with `[mechanism]` or `[prose-only]`, and none says "not examined". No placeholder pin appears anywhere.

The three transitions with guard `none` (t5, t7, t8) store `agent` in `guard_evaluated_by`, because the field has no "nobody" value. A `model-limit` finding says this. A `could-not-run` finding names the failure and retry edges t2, t5, t7 and t8.

The tests are in `crates/athena-cap-study/src/rules.rs`. They read the study files and answer the rules' git questions from `pinned-source/`. They check that:
- every rule passes;
- `validation.json` equals what the rules return;
- a wrong SHA, a changed quote or a bad line range is flagged;
- no placeholder pin appears, and every claim is tagged;
- a guard of `none` is never marked as evaluated by code.

One of my own citations was off by a line, and the test caught it before I finished.

I also added the `studies/**` row to `docs/non-rust-files.md`, a CHANGELOG entry, and decision D78 in `docs/decisions.md`.
